<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chhoto Sona Mosque</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Small Golden Mosque, Choto Sona Masjid</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Chhoto Sona Mosque, the Small Golden Mosque, is a mosque at Shibganj in Chapai Nawabganj district, Bangladesh, on the site of the old city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaur">Gaur</a>. It was built during the reign of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alauddin-husain-shah">Alauddin Husain Shah</a>, between 1493 and 1519, of brick faced with carved stone. Its fifteen domes were once gilded, and it is regarded as one of the finest works of the Bengal Sultanate.</p></div>
